That's a matter of game play and how much you revisit levels.
I often make sure it's safe to pray before leaving any co-aligned
and/or convertable altar.  So during much of my play I know it's
safe to pray and I know how to avoid most of the emergencies
that call for risky prayer.  I also often head for the nearest altar
after an emergency prayer to make sure it's safe to pray again.

Going from DL=26 back to minetown is a long way to shuttle,
but if there aren't any nearest altars, I've done it.

Because I use altars like this and because I use wands of
enlightenment, I think prayer beads are redundant.

If prayer beads came with a number of charges, and the number
was small like fire/cold horn not large like tinning-kit/camera
then it becomes an alternative to a wand of enlightenment.  It
becomes one more chargable thing competing for those rare
scrolls, or it becomes one more thing to waste a charge from
the Platinum card that might have been used on a death wand.


